{
  "title": "Gradient of a single neuron",
  "function": "neuron_grad",
  "params": [
    {
      "name": "x",
      "type": "float"
    },
    {
      "name": "w",
      "type": "float"
    },
    {
      "name": "b",
      "type": "float"
    }
  ],
  "returns": "vec",
  "library": true,
  "hints": [
    "Name the middle step: z = w·x + b, then y = σ(z). The chain rule says ∂y/∂w = σ'(z) · ∂z/∂w.",
    "∂z/∂w = x, ∂z/∂b = 1, and ∂z/∂x = w.",
    "Compute s = sigmoid_derivative(w*x + b) once, then return [s*x, s, s*w]."
  ],
  "tests": [
    {
      "args": [
        1,
        0,
        0
      ],
      "description": "z = 0, where σ' = ¼",
      "expected": [
        0.25,
        0.25,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "args": [
        2,
        0.5,
        -1
      ],
      "description": "z = 2·0.5 − 1 = 0 again, but now x = 2",
      "expected": [
        0.5,
        0.25,
        0.125
      ]
    },
    {
      "args": [
        -1.5,
        2,
        0.5
      ],
      "description": "a negative input",
      "hidden": true,
      "expected": [
        -0.10515557481766225,
        0.07010371654510816,
        0.14020743309021633
      ]
    },
    {
      "args": [
        3,
        -1,
        1
      ],
      "description": "a negative weight",
      "hidden": true,
      "expected": [
        0.3149807562105195,
        0.1049935854035065,
        -0.1049935854035065
      ]
    },
    {
      "args": [
        0,
        5,
        0
      ],
      "description": "x = 0 means the weight gets no gradient",
      "hidden": true,
      "expected": [
        0.0,
        0.25,
        1.25
      ]
    }
  ]
}
